			'title' => 'The Best Grass Types for Houston Lawns',
			'slug' => 'best-grass-for-houston',
			'excerpt' => 'St. Augustine, Bermuda, or Zoysia? How to choose the right warm-season grass for your property.',
			'category' => 'Grass Selection',
			'hero' => 'https://d64gsuwffb70l.cloudfront.net/6a0d29e1debea06021d065ea_1779247745126_1332fe27.jpg',
			'content_main' => '<p>St. Augustine is the dominant residential grass in Houston for one reason: it tolerates the partial shade of mature trees, performs in our heat and humidity, and delivers the lush, broad-leaf look most homeowners want.</p>',
			'content_second' => '<p>Bermuda is the right call for full-sun lots, sports turf, and commercial frontages where high traffic and rapid recovery matter more than texture.</p>

<p>Zoysia is the premium upgrade — denser, finer, softer underfoot. It costs more, but on the right property it delivers a country-club finish nothing else matches.</p>',
