		array(
			'title' => 'When Should You Install Sod in Houston?',
			'slug' => 'when-to-install-sod-houston',
			'excerpt' => 'The honest answer: nearly any month works in Houston — but each season has tradeoffs.',
			'category' => 'Installation',
			'hero' => 'https://d64gsuwffb70l.cloudfront.net/6a0d29e1debea06021d065ea_1779247769692_9f6dd6ac.jpg',
			'content_main' => '<p>Houston is one of the few US markets where sod can be installed essentially year-round. Our warm-season grasses establish quickest from April through October when soil temperatures are reliably above 65°F.</p>

<p>Winter installs (December–February) are possible and often cheaper, but expect dormant, brown turf until spring green-up. The roots are still establishing — the green color just shows up later.</p>',
			'content_second' => '<p>If your timing is flexible, late spring through early summer is the sweet spot: warm soil, regular rain, and a full growing season ahead for the lawn to root in before its first stress test.</p>',
