		array(
			'title' => 'How to Care for Sod After Installation',
			'slug' => 'sod-care-after-installation',
			'excerpt' => 'The first 30 days make or break a new lawn. Here is the simple, no-nonsense schedule we hand to every client.',
			'category' => 'Care & Maintenance',
			'hero' => 'https://d64gsuwffb70l.cloudfront.net/6a0d29e1debea06021d065ea_1779247846886_7f420ca0.jpg',
			'content_main' => '<p>Days 1–7: Water heavily, twice daily. Your goal is to keep the soil under the sod consistently moist — not soggy, not dry. The roots are knitting into the soil during this window.</p>',
			'content_second' => '<p>Days 8–21: Back off to once daily, longer cycles. The roots are reaching down for water now, so you want to encourage them.</p>

<p>Day 21+: Transition to a normal Houston schedule — 2–3 deeper waterings per week, depending on rainfall and temperature. First mow happens around day 14–21, taking off no more than the top third of the blade.</p>',
